1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,370
Singer-songwriters write songs, but how do they do it?
创作型歌手写歌，但他们是怎样做到的呢？

2
00:00:04,370 --> 00:00:07,500
Where do musicians get their inspiration from?
音乐家们的灵感从何而来？

3
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:11,180
What comes first – the music or the lyrics?
哪个先出现——是音乐还是歌词？

4
00:00:11,180 --> 00:00:16,210
It turns out that everyone has their own way of writing which works for them.
事实证明，每个人都有自己行之有效的创作方式。

5
00:00:16,210 --> 00:00:20,040
Bob Dylan is a musician with a unique musical style.
鲍勃·迪伦是一位有着独特音乐风格的音乐家。

6
00:00:20,040 --> 00:00:25,770
It has been described as folk rock, gospel, country and jazz.
这种风格被描述为民谣摇滚、福音、乡村和爵士。

7
00:00:25,770 --> 00:00:34,160
He told the BBC that he gets a lot of his writing inspiration from novels like Don Quixote and Robinson Crusoe.
他告诉BBC，他的许多创作灵感来自《堂吉诃德》和《鲁滨逊漂流记》这样的小说。

8
00:00:34,160 --> 00:00:41,890
He said 'They give you a way of looking at life and understanding of human nature and a standard to measure things by.
他说："它们提供给你一种看待生活的方式，对人性的理解，以及衡量事物的标准。

9
00:00:41,890 --> 00:00:45,650
I took that all with me when I started composing lyrics'.
当我开始创作歌词时，我把这些都考虑在内。"

10
00:00:45,650 --> 00:00:47,700
It seems to have worked for him.
这似乎对他很管用。

11
00:00:47,700 --> 00:00:53,800
He has had a career spanning six decades and has won many songwriting awards.
他的职业生涯跨越了六十年，赢得了许多歌曲创作奖项。

12
00:00:53,800 --> 00:00:57,630
And what comes first, the music or the lyrics?
那么哪个先出现，是音乐还是歌词？

13
00:00:57,630 --> 00:01:11,110
Stephen Sondheim, a musical theatre composer who died in 2021, said in an interview with The New Yorker that, when it comes to songwriting, the stress in a phrase is very important for him.
已于2021年去世的音乐剧作曲家斯蒂芬·桑德海姆在接受《纽约客》采访时表示，对于歌曲创作来说，短语中的重音对他来说非常重要。"

14
00:01:11,110 --> 00:01:22,410
'You can start writing a lyric, and then the inflection of the lyric suggests a tune.' Therefore, in his way of writing, the music and lyrics come at roughly the same time.
你可以开始写一句歌词，然后歌词的语调变化会使人想到一段旋律。"因此，在他的创作方式中，音乐和歌词大致是同时出现的。

15
00:01:22,410 --> 00:01:28,800
In 2022, Taylor Swift won a Songwriter-Artist of the Decade award.
2022年，泰勒·斯威夫特获得了"十年词曲创作人-艺术家奖"。

16
00:01:28,800 --> 00:01:33,850
In her speech, she said lyrics are her favourite part of songwriting.
在她的获奖感言中，她说歌词是她歌曲创作中最喜欢的部分。

17
00:01:33,850 --> 00:01:47,210
She describes the majority of her songs as having a 'modern storyline or references, with a poetic twist' and commonly uses real life experiences and conversations as influence.
她将自己的大部分歌曲描述为"夹杂诗意的现代故事情节或引用"，并且通常以现实生活经历和对话作为灵感来源。

18
00:01:47,210 --> 00:01:53,150
Aside from lyrics, an important part of many songs is the instrumental backing.
除了歌词，许多歌曲的一个重要部分是器乐伴奏。

19
00:01:53,150 --> 00:02:01,280
This is often created with chords, where at least three notes are played at the same time, often on a piano or guitar.
这通常由和弦构成，即至少三个音同时奏响，常在钢琴或吉他上演奏。

20
00:02:01,280 --> 00:02:09,120
Chord progression is where different chords are played one after the other, and therefore can act as the base for vocals.
和弦进行是指不同的和弦依次奏响，因此可以作为人声的基础。

21
00:02:09,120 --> 00:02:15,760
So, if you're feeling musical, lay down some chords, get inspired and give it a go yourself!
所以，如果你有音乐灵感，那就录制一些和弦，寻找灵感，亲自尝试一下吧！
